===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} Something that is [[tough]], or [[difficult]].
#: ''His question is a '''toughie'''. I might have to do some more research.''
# Someone or something that  is [[strong]] and [[resilient]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1977|month=October|work=Organic Gardening and Farming |title=Two Old Houseplant Toughies |author=Gladys Reed Robinson|volume=24|page=170|passage=Sansevieria and aspidistra are two old houseplant '''toughies''' that make good indoor choices.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1996| title=Laurie and Claire |author=Kathleen Rowntree | page=319| passage=With typical courage she had taken hold of her life and changed it for the better. She always was a brave little '''toughie''', and now her courage had paid off. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017| title=The Silent Corner|author=Dean Koontz| page=84| passage=His eyes were red, but his lashes were not beaded with fresh tears. He was something, this little '''toughie'''.}}
# A [[tough]]; Someone or something that acts as a [[thug]] or [[bully]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1936|month=April|work=The Modern Monthly |title=Hitler and Mussolini Win Again|author=|volume=9|number=9|page=3|passage=The liberal states, in the present situation, are the "softies"; the Fascist states are the "'''toughies'''". And the '''toughies''' are always able to get away with "murder" until the softies become tough.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2001| title=Shanghai Quartet: The Crossings of Four Women of China |author=Min-Zhan Lu | page=249| passage=But we knew she would follow how and why my student and I would immediately detect the similarity in our situation from the studied calmness we had both displayed toward the havoc roused by the '''toughies''' to intimidate the new female temporary teacher.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012| title=Virgin With Butterflies|author=Tom Powers | page=| passage=There was Butch behind the bar, and there sat four of the '''toughies''' at their table with their heads all close together and not drunk no more.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012| title=Sons, Daughters and Wine Tasters |author=Jules Lombard | page=11| passage=Often I don't even have a partner when I make my rounds as a patrol cop, because of city budget constraints. But when the '''toughie''' is armed or there are too many '''toughies''', l have to call for a backup before I make a move. }}




